      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`Qwen3MoeDecoderLayer` builds its sparse MoE block with a hard-coded `Qwen3MoeSparseMoeBlock(...)`, while the model level already lets callers inject `decoder_layer_type`. A downstream layer subclass that only needs a different MoE block forward today has to either re-implement the whole `__init__` (as `MellumDecoderLayer` does for attention) or reassign `self.mlp.__class__` after construction to keep the loaded experts.\n\nThis adds `moe_block_type: type[nn.Module] = Qwen3MoeSparseMoeBlock` to the layer constructor, mirroring `decoder_layer_type`. Default behaviour is unchanged.\n\nDownstream use: vLLM-Omni's opt-in HF-numerics mode for the Qwen3-Omni thinker (true on-policy RL, verl-project/verl-omni#637), which subclasses the layer and the MoE block.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nNo behaviour change for existing callers: the default argument is the class that was hard-coded. `pre-commit run --files vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_moe.py`.\n\n## Test Result\n\nruff / ruff format clean. Qwen3-MoE model construction and weight loading exercised downstream through the vLLM-Omni subclass on a 4-layer Qwen3-Omni-30B-A3B thinker.\n\nAI assistance was used for this change. I reviewed every line.\n",
